<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/000X">Example <span data-tag="000X">1.2.4.3</span>.</a> The horn $\Lambda ^{1}_{0} \subset \Delta ^1$ is the vertex $\{ 0\} $, and the horn $\Lambda ^{1}_{1} \subset \Delta ^1$ is the vertex $\{ 1\} $ (see Example <a data-tag="000Q" href="/tag/000Q">1.1.0.15</a>). In particular, $\Lambda ^{1}_{0}$ and $\Lambda ^{1}_{1}$ are abstractly isomorphic to the standard $0$-simplex $\Delta ^{0}$. Moreover, the boundary $\operatorname{\partial \Delta }^{1}$ is the disjoint union of $\Lambda ^{1}_{0}$ and $\Lambda ^{1}_{1}$. </p>
